+Prompt acceptance is identified by the existing user-source `rpcId`. Session Controller checks both current inboxes and durable inbox insertions, so a network retry cannot resurrect a message that was claimed or explicitly removed. It repeats the check after asynchronous attachment admission and immediately before the synchronous inbox insertion. This uses the Session log as the receipt instead of maintaining a second mutation registry; an admission that fails before insertion may retry with the same identity. Concurrent attachment preparation can still produce unreferenced content-addressed objects, but only one prompt enters the inbox.
